  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 13 items, 6 patients, all closed. Each patient got one reply saying what was done.\n\n- Gloria Hayes (pt-0026), 2 messages, both about lisinopril 20 mg: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0001). The Oct 5 potassium of 6.1 came from a hemolyzed sample, so it doesn't count. The latest valid potassium is 4.6 (Apr 14 BMP). Repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0002).\n- Frank Odum (pt-0027):\n  - Lisinopril 10 mg: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0006). The outside potassium of 5.9 (St. Brigid, collected Aug 27) was hemolyzed, so it doesn't count. The latest valid potassium is 4.5 (Jan 20 BMP). Repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0008).\n  - Amlodipine 5 mg: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0007) under §4; last completed visit was Jan 2026.\n- Lena Park (pt-0028):\n  - Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply, no refills (mr-t0012), plus BMP (sr-t0013). Her last BMP was collected 10/2/2025 (scanned 11/3), which is more than 12 months ago. Her last visit was 7/20/2026.\n  - Metformin (pharmacy request): not refilled. Her latest valid eGFR is 39: the 7/20 result was corrected on 7/24 from the 51 cited in the progress note. Urgent task sent to you (task-t0014, about mr-00287). Current order left active.\n- Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029):\n  - Lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled. Her BMP 17 days after the 9/21 dose increase showed creatinine 1.24, up 38% from 0.90. Under §2 that counts the same as a potassium of 5.5 or higher. Urgent task sent to you (task-t0018, about mr-00291). She has been out of lisinopril since 10/20. Current order left active.\n  - Metformin 1000 mg: 30-day supply, no refills (mr-t0019), plus HbA1c ordered (sr-t0020). Her eGFR is 54, but her last HbA1c was collected 4/14/2026, more than 6 months ago.\n- Samuel Price (pt-0030), 3 messages:\n  - Lisinopril 20 mg: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0024). Potassium was 5.2 on 10/6, and creatinine rose 24% after the dose increase, under the 30% limit.\n  - Metformin: the patient and pharmacy requests were treated as one, with a single order for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0025). eGFR is 65, and an outside HbA1c collected 8/19/2026 is within 6 months.\n- Marcus Webb (pt-0031):\n  - Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply, no refills (mr-t0030), plus BMP (sr-t0031). His last BMP was collected 10/20/2025, more than 12 months ago. His last visit was 9/28/2026.\n  - Metformin 500 mg: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0032). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error (mislabelled specimen). His valid eGFR of 92 and HbA1c of 6.9 are both from 9/28.\n\nTwo urgent tasks are waiting for your review: Brooks (lisinopril, currently out) and Park (metformin).",
